{
 "version": 1,
 "meta": {
  "title": "fig-boot-why",
  "description": "Tap 6 with the isolation FET Qi off. Left: its gate-drain and drain-source capacitance, about 0.8 nF, go from I minus to nodes held at I+, which slows tap 6 to 236 kHz at the ADC. Right: Qb and Rtih tie the gate and ihi to a follower that copies the voltage of I minus, so no current flows through them."
 },
